idsize Business (SMB)","description":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#graze-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"graze-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:47:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:49+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Graze continually improves its customers’ experience by staying agile—including in its infrastructure. The company sells healthy snacks through its website and via U.K. retailers. It runs all its infrastructure on AWS, including its customer-facing websites and all its internal systems from the factory floor to business intelligence.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Graze_Customer-Reference_Logo.470b1dc2ecf70dd701bb6608fe90fd5ce149d11c.png","displayLocation":"United Kingdom","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"Read the Graze customer case study, powered by the AWS cloud. AWS provides cloud computing services to hundreds of thousands of customers. ","industry":"Retail","sortDate":"2016-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/graze/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Graze","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2016","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Graze Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Lambda","description":"AWS Lambda","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:46+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Redshift","description":"Amazon Redshift","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:56+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-