Block Store (EBS)","description":"Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#ssa","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Sub-Saharan Africa","description":"Sub-Saharan Africa","dateCreated":"2020-03-10T05:18:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:58+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#industry#travel-and-hospitality","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"travel-and-hospitality","description":"\u003cp\u003eAs of 4/2023, this tag is initially being used specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/travel-and-hospitality/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can switch to the AND operator, enabling them to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2019-07-17T22:21:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:41:02+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#smb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","description":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#aws-case-study-medstar-health","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"aws-case-study-medstar-health","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:50:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-12T01:35:27+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"MedStar Health, the largest not-for-profit healthcare system in Maryland and the Washington, D.C., region, wanted to offer patients an easy way to search for doctors, medical services, and locations, and to make appointments. By creating a centralized patient engagement portal on AWS, MedStar has increased website availability and page download speeds, while lowering monthly operating costs for the portal by more than 40 percent.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/logos/600x400_logos/600x400_MedstarHealth_Logo.98b4b1c1a2e2cfbaabe0efd87a81e4d7f41440c8.png","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eMedStar Health, the largest not-for-profit healthcare system in Maryland and the Washington, D.C., region, wanted to offer patients an easy way to search for doctors, medical services, and locations, and to make appointments. To deliver a patient-first experience, the healthcare system decided to combine its disparate websites into a single, searchable portal using AWS. By creating a centralized patient engagement portal on AWS, MedStar has dramatically increased website availability and page download speeds, while lowering monthly operating costs for the portal by more than 40 percent.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Healthcare","sortDate":"2015-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/medstar-health/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"MedStar Health","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2015","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"AWS Case Study: MedStar Health"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Content Delivery","description":"Content Deliv